  "instance_name": "audience_id",
  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience is individuals who hold or are exposed to xenophobic and nationalistic stereotypes about Romanian people, particularly those who may be predisposed to believe that people from Romania are inherently dishonest or greedy, regardless of their socioeconomic status. The meme is designed to provoke negative sentiment toward Romanian nationals by leveraging harmful generalizations and visual tropes (e.g., the elderly woman evoking pity, which is then undermined by the accusation of theft). The intended audience likely includes people who are already familiar with or receptive to anti-Romanian stereotypes, and who may be motivated by nationalist or economically resentful attitudes. The meme’s use of the contrast between Romania and London also targets audiences who perceive Eastern European countries as economically disadvantaged but morally suspect, reinforcing a community-specific narrative of 'outsider' exploitation.",
